package localized

// NLS-P10 review — a QUERY with a localised description. It lives here rather than in
// `er.ttr` only because queries are authored in the db file by convention (see the
// bundled `model-ttr/*/db.ttr`).
//
// Why it is worth a fixture: `ModelBundleQuery` carries TWO ObjectDescriptors for the
// same query — its own, and the one nested inside `QueryDescriptor`. The first shipped
// locale-selected and the second did not, so a bilingual query described itself in
// Czech at one field and not at all at the other. The spec pins both.
def query bilingual_query {
    description: { cs: "Dvojjazyčný dotaz", en: "A bilingual query" },
    language: SQL,
    sourceText: """SELECT 1"""
}
